    "thm-finite-action-gibbs-policy-optimum": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-kl-regularized-policy-improvement",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $Y$ be a finite nonempty set. A probability vector on $Y$ is a family $p=(p_y)_{y\\in Y}$ with $p_y\\ge0$ and $\\sum_{y\\in Y}p_y=1$. For probability vectors $p,q$, define the finite relative entropy\n$$D(p\\|q)=\\sum_{y:p_y>0}p_y\\log\\frac{p_y}{q_y}$$\nwhen $p_y=0$ whenever $q_y=0$, and define $D(p\\|q)=+\\infty$ otherwise. Terms with $p_y=0$ are omitted. Given a real reward $r:Y\\to\\mathbb R$ and a coefficient $\\beta>0$, define\n$$F_{q,r,\\beta}(p)=\\sum_{y\\in Y}p_y r(y)-\\beta D(p\\|q).$$\nThe finite KL-regularized policy-improvement problem is to maximize $F_{q,r,\\beta}$ over all probability vectors $p$ on $Y$. The reference $q$ has full support when $q_y>0$ for every $y\\in Y$; in that case $F_{q,r,\\beta}(p)$ is finite for every $p$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1",
            "3.1",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-proper-scoring-rule",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "For an integer $K\\ge2$, let the label set be $\\mathcal Y=\\{1,\\ldots,K\\}$ and let $\\Delta_K=\\{q\\in[0,1]^K:\\sum_{j=1}^Kq_j=1\\}$. A finite-label score loss is a function $S:\\Delta_K\\times\\mathcal Y\\to[0,+\\infty]$ whose section $q\\mapsto S(q,j)$ is Borel measurable for every label $j$. If the true label distribution is $p\\in\\Delta_K$ and the reported forecast is $q\\in\\Delta_K$, its expected score loss is $\\bar S(p,q)=\\sum_{j=1}^Kp_jS(q,j)$, where a term with $p_j=0$ contributes zero even when $S(q,j)=+\\infty$. The loss is **proper** if $\\bar S(p,p)\\le\\bar S(p,q)$ for every $p,q\\in\\Delta_K$, and **strictly proper** if equality implies $q=p$. The logarithmic loss is $S_{\\log}(q,j)=-\\log q_j$, with $-\\log0=+\\infty$, where $\\log$ is the natural logarithm; the Brier loss is $S_{\\mathrm B}(q,j)=\\sum_{i=1}^K(q_i-\\mathbf1_{\\{i=j\\}})^2$.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "thm-log-and-brier-strict-propriety",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For every $K\\ge2$ and $p,q\\in\\Delta_K$, the logarithmic and Brier losses in the definition of finite-label score loss satisfy $\\bar S(p,p)\\le\\bar S(p,q)$, with equality only when $q=p$. The expected logarithmic loss at the truthful forecast is finite, including when some coordinates of $p$ vanish.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
