          "step": "1.1",
          "claim": "Since $Y$ is finite and each $q_y e^{r(y)/\\beta}$ is a positive finite real, their sum $Z$ is positive and finite. The coordinates of $p^*$ are positive and sum to $1$, so $p^*$ is a full-support probability vector.",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "gibbs-objective-gap",
          "step": "2.1",
          "claim": "For each $y$, the definition of $p^*$ gives $\\log(p_y^*/q_y)=r(y)/\\beta-\\log Z$. Substitution into the finite sum for $D(p\\|p^*)$, omitting zero coordinates of $p$, yields $\\beta D(p\\|p^*)=\\beta D(p\\|q)-\\sum_y p_y r(y)+\\beta\\log Z=\\beta\\log Z-F_{q,r,\\beta}(p)$. All sums are finite, and all logarithm arguments in the sums are positive.",
